<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Culture &amp; Lifestyle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-cul" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1441?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb2ae01da0f689c349308c3c5aff89bb5f7de34bcee901147b7d544677753388</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--e5a64327dbec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. People forget that, over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What does Saxony-Anhalt's election mean for migrants?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3e721ad30d301bd0ee052c9629f5fff8e0f92de908d65cc80950461c4ef13a0</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:57Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553--f0f67d52d4b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-saxony-anhalt-s-election-mean-for-migrants/a-78504553?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD could make history in the German state of Saxony-Anhalt. For many people with a migration background, the September 6 state election raises questions about belonging, security and their future in Germany.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Influential humanists: These are the winners of the Goethe Medal 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e1c84a66b1549ab82829852dae1a973b9c8033b41d7492267cacc12fa691630</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975--15befdde29df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The prestigious German cultural award recognizes the artistic work and commitment to cultural dialogue of Arvo Pärt, Anita Raja and Prodromos Tsinikoris.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Japanese artist Yayoi Kusama dies at 97</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39f5e866834cdde29d39d7a69036740099402112b85b78fb3dca14b4fb129d62</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T02:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japanese-artist-yayoi-kusama-dies-at-97/a-78518473--64dc695506be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japanese-artist-yayoi-kusama-dies-at-97/a-78518473?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From works of "self-obliteration" to polka dotted nudes, the pioneering artist developed a unique body of work likely to be relevant for years to come.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>At Venice Film Festival, politics take center stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f4384cf5023b360f042235a994d04089ddcaf33c2c2a5b072817e4f8aafb539</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761--44d85d609652.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With works about Gaza, Ukraine and Elon Musk, political cinema is in the spotlight at the 2026 Venice Film Festival.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1210e49270c6443f47d2f6eb7020abe60c30ab8dd1ec06f4c6aaf45ab8ee69</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--7a39d99408d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaf4a9757858e4f3796c0fe944e3d793b4af13346064d10b227edda5c7d58775</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--7e7431cf0f1b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bauhaus Manifesto: Broad alliance promoting artistic freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcf63999e9251109eee8f22b2ec5abab8708c60530014dedd1caf446812da8b8</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T10:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460--32fdb92cab89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weeks before Saxony-Anhalt's state election, representatives from German cultural, crafts, architecture, design and church sectors unite to promote freedom, openness and creativity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Hunger stones: The history behind 'if you see me, weep'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543fe6fc2c925dfb7e7e29af5bca06f651aa70dcb52435f062ab87892e250a8a</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T07:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hunger-stones-the-history-behind-if-you-see-me-weep/a-78345729--a65d352c5848.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hunger-stones-the-history-behind-if-you-see-me-weep/a-78345729?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Centuries-old hunger stones are emerging as Europe's rivers recede. Among the most famous is the Decin hunger stone in the Elbe River with its cryptic message.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da3edc47c755557b907f439523580c119d5c0697b4479d34660710aa82ac3db5</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578-